      "name": "Sébastiani's Cavalry",
      "formation": "II Reserve Cavalry Corps",
      "side": "French",
      "summary": "Camped carelessly on Murat's left, it was surprised at dawn by Orlov-Denisov's Cossacks, lost its guns and baggage and was driven back, rallying only when Murat led his cavalry against the Russian regulars.",
      "notes": [
        "Murat, the book's named commander, led the advance guard and rallied this cavalry himself.",
        "After Nafziger's order of battle for Borodino, where these brigades were Pajol's division; by October the reserve cavalry was a few hundred horse a regiment, so all are Small. Sébastiani commanded the corps at Tarutino.",
        "Three Light Cavalry Brigades and no infantry show as historical departures.",
        "Commanders are at Staff Rating 8, the default for historical forces, except the book's named Marshal Murat, with his own rating."
